<body>

<!-- HEADER -->
<div class="report-header">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="badge">Trend Analysis Report · April 2026</div>
    <h1>BIEK Computer Science<br>HSC Part-2 Past Paper Analysis</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A comprehensive examination of question type distribution, volume shifts, and topic patterns across 11 years (2015–2025) of BIEK 12th Class Computer Science past papers — enabling data-driven curriculum alignment and exam preparation strategies.</p>
    <div class="kpi-bar">
      <div class="kpi-card"><span class="val">327</span><span class="lbl">Total Questions</span></div>
      <div class="kpi-card"><span class="val">10</span><span class="lbl">Exam Years</span></div>
      <div class="kpi-card"><span class="val">3</span><span class="lbl">Question Types</span></div>
      <div class="kpi-card"><span class="val">33.3</span><span class="lbl">Avg Qs/Year</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- NAV -->
<nav class="toc">
  <div class="container">
    <ul>
      <li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
      <li><a href="#yearly">Year-by-Year Volume</a></li>
      <li><a href="#types">Question Type Trends</a></li>
      <li><a href="#topics">Topic Patterns</a></li>
      <li><a href="#insights">Strategic Insights</a></li>
      <li><a href="#conclusions">Conclusions</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</nav>

<!-- ===== SECTION 1: OVERVIEW ===== -->
<div class="container">
<section id="overview">
  <div class="section-label">Section 01</div>
  <h2>Dataset &amp; Examination Overview</h2>
  <p class="lead">This report is based on a community-compiled dataset of 327 questions drawn from BIEK Computer Science Paper-II (HSC Part-2) examinations spanning 2015 to 2025. The dataset covers 10 distinct exam years — 2020 data is absent from the source dataset.</p>

  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="stat-card">
      <div class="num">327</div>
      <div class="desc">Total questions across all years</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-card green">
      <div class="num">150</div>
      <div class="desc">MCQs (45.9% of total)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-card orange">
      <div class="num">147</div>
      <div class="desc">Short Questions (44.9% of total)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-card purple">
      <div class="num">30</div>
      <div class="desc">Long Questions (9.2% of total)</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Structural Architecture of the Exam</h3>
  <p>Each examined year follows a consistent three-part structure: a fixed block of 15 Multiple Choice Questions (MCQs), a variable block of short-answer questions, and exactly 3 long-answer questions. The most notable structural distinction across the dataset's timeline is the evolution of the short-question count — which increased and then contracted, marking three identifiable phases.</p>

  <div class="phase-band">
    <div class="phase-seg p1">
      <div class="ph-label">Phase 1: Foundation</div>
      <div>2015–2016</div>
      <div style="font-size:12px; margin-top:4px;">27 Qs/year · 9 Short Qs</div>
    </div>
    <div class="phase-seg p2">
      <div class="ph-label">Phase 2: Expansion</div>
      <div>2017–2019</div>
      <div style="font-size:12px; margin-top:4px;">36 Qs/year · 18 Short Qs</div>
    </div>
    <div class="phase-seg p3">
      <div class="ph-label">Phase 3: Consolidation</div>
      <div>2021–2025</div>
      <div style="font-size:12px; margin-top:4px;">33 Qs/year · 15 Short Qs</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Key structural constant:</strong> MCQs have been exactly 15 per year and Long Questions exactly 3 per year throughout the entire 11-year span. The only variable element is the short-question count, which changed twice: from 9 (2015–2016) to 18 (2017–2019), then settling at 15 (2021–present).
  </div>

  <h3>Data Source &amp; Quality</h3>
  <p>The dataset (<code>cs-12th-question-bank-biek-su.csv</code>) was sourced from Kaggle (user: sadamumer), derived from official BIEK papers and publicly scanned past papers. It contains 4 columns: <code>id</code>, <code>year</code>, <code>type</code>, and <code>question</code>. The question text uses a <code>$</code> delimiter to separate MCQ options and long-question sub-parts. The dataset does not distinguish between annual and supplementary examination sittings, and <strong>2020 data is entirely absent</strong>.</p>
</section>

<!-- ===== SECTION 2: YEARLY DISTRIBUTION ===== -->
<section id="yearly">
  <div class="section-label">Section 02</div>
  <h2>Year-by-Year Question Volume Analysis</h2>
  <p class="lead">Total question counts shifted meaningfully over the 10 examined years, driven exclusively by changes in the short-question quota. MCQ and Long question counts remained static — a testament to the exam board's commitment to structural predictability in those components.</p>

  <!-- Line chart: total questions per year -->
  <div class="chart-wrap">
    <div class="chart-title">Total Questions per Exam Year (2015–2025)</div>
    <div class="chart-sub">Note: 2020 data is absent from the source dataset and is excluded from this analysis.</div>
    <canvas id="totalLineChart" height="80"></canvas>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-row">
    <!-- Bar chart: breakdown per year -->
    <div class="chart-wrap">
      <div class="chart-title">Question Type Breakdown by Year</div>
      <div class="chart-sub">Stacked absolute counts — MCQs (blue), Short (green), Long (orange)</div>
      <canvas id="stackedBarChart" height="160"></canvas>
    </div>
    <!-- YoY Change -->
    <div class="chart-wrap">
      <div class="chart-title">Year-over-Year Change in Total Question Count</div>
      <div class="chart-sub">Absolute change compared to preceding exam year in dataset</div>
      <canvas id="yoyChart" height="160"></canvas>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Detailed Year-by-Year Data Table</h3>
  <table class="data-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Year</th>
        <th>MCQs</th>
        <th>Short Qs</th>
        <th>Long Qs</th>
        <th>Total</th>
        <th>YoY Change</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>2015</strong></td><td>15</td><td>9</td><td>3</td><td><strong>27</strong></td><td><span class="pill pill-nc">Baseline</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>2016</strong></td><td>15</td><td>9</td><td>3</td><td><strong>27</strong></td><td><span class="pill pill-nc">0 (0.0%)</span></td></tr>
