  <h3>Key Observations</h3>
  <p><strong>The 2017 spike is the single most significant structural event in this dataset.</strong> The short-question count doubled from 9 to 18, increasing the total paper length by 33.3% (from 27 to 36 questions). This expansion was sustained for three years (2017–2019) before being trimmed to 15 short questions in 2021 — a reduction of 3 questions (−8.3%) that has held stable through 2025.</p>
  <p>The data reveals that once the board sets a question count pattern, it maintains it for multi-year periods. The current 33-question format (15 MCQ + 15 Short + 3 Long) represents the longest unbroken stable run in the dataset, now in its 5th consecutive year since 2021.</p>
