  <h2>Strategic Insights for Exam Preparation</h2>
  <p class="lead">The following recommendations are drawn directly from the data patterns identified above. They are organized by audience and priority level based on historical question frequency and structural stability.</p>

  <h3>For Students: Preparation Priorities</h3>
  <div class="insight-grid">
    <div class="insight-card green">
      <div class="ic-title"><span class="tag-icon green">1</span>Master C Functions (Highest Priority)</div>
      <div class="ic-body">Functions appear in all 10 years across all three question types. Know: defining functions, function prototypes, call-by-value vs. call-by-reference, user-defined functions, and recursion. Program-writing on functions is a near-certain short/long question.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="insight-card green">
      <div class="ic-title"><span class="tag-icon green">2</span>All Loop Types in C</div>
      <div class="ic-body">for, while, do-while, and nested loops appear in 9/10 years. Practice writing programs with each, converting between loop types, and tracing output. Nested loops and loop-based programs (tables, series, patterns) are perennial staples.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="insight-card green">
      <div class="ic-title"><span class="tag-icon green">3</span>Database Keys (Primary, Foreign, Composite)</div>
      <div class="ic-body">Present in all 10 years. Questions frequently ask to distinguish between key types, explain usage, and relate to referential integrity. Since 2023, candidate key, super key, and alternate key have also appeared — expand prep accordingly.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="insight-card">
      <div class="ic-title"><span class="tag-icon">4</span>C Operators (All Categories)</div>
      <div class="ic-body">Arithmetic, relational, logical, assignment, and increment/decrement operators appear in 9/10 years. From 2025, bitwise and ternary operators are also being tested. Know operator precedence — a recurring short question.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="insight-card">
      <div class="ic-title"><span class="tag-icon">5</span>Database Models &amp; DBMS Concepts</div>
      <div class="ic-body">Hierarchical, relational, and network models appear repeatedly. DBMS advantages, DBA roles, DDL/DML/DCL/SQL, and MS Access objects (table, query, form, report, macro, module) appear across all phases. This is the second dominant content pillar.</div>
